WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:06.370
The Huns played an instrumental part in destroying
the Western Roman Empire, the Avars brought

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.860
the Eastern Roman Empire to almost the same
fate, the Khazars stopped Arab expansion across

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.650
the Caucasus while in the process drastically
weakening the Umayyad Caliphate, and the Nomads

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.560
of the Mongol Steppe were such a threat to
China that numerous Chinese dynasties all

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.800
across the ages spent enormous amounts of
resources on large wall building projects

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.750
just to keep the Nomads out.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:33.000
It is undeniable that the early medieval nomads
of the Eurasian Steppe had a tremendous impact

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.410
on Euroasian history and, therefore, it would
be nice to know how these nomads lived in

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.260
the steppe, especially since a lot of what
we know about them isn’t very accurate.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.160
Before we delve into the complicated life
of the early medieval Euroasian steppe quote

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.840
unquote “nomads”, we have to talk about
the polities that existed in the steppe during

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.190
this time just to give some background.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:57.990
We will start off in the 6th century with
the First Turkic Khaganate.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.329
There were many nomadic polities before then
but we have to start off somewhere and the

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:07.150
First Turkic Khaganate is a perfect starting
point as it gave rise to many nomadic groups

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.150
that influenced Eurasian politics for the
rest of the medieval period.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:16.210
The First Turkic Khaganate emerged after the
Gokturks, an early Turkic tribe, successfully

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:22.350
rebelled against their Rouran overlords and
took control of their state in 552.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.610
Subsequently Gokturks went on to conquer much
of the Euroasian steppe.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:31.260
The Gokturks came as far as the Byzantine
controlled Crimea in 576 and even laid siege

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.270
to the city of Chersonesus, today’s Sewastopol.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.220
The Avars that came to Pannonia during the
6th century and established the Avar Khaganate

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.580
were fleeing from the Gokturk conquest.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.260
There is a theory that the Avars were the
Rouran that were defeated by the Gokturks

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.420
and fled west, however, this is hard to prove.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.880
The Avars could have easily been one of the
many nomadic tribes in the steppe that just

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.799
didn’t want to get conquered by the First
Turkic Khaganate.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:59.900
Nonetheless, wherever they came from, the
Avars, along the way to Pannonia, subdued

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.590
the Bulgar tribes living around the Don river.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.840
In c. 584 a succession crisis in the First
Turkic Khaganate led to a civil war which

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.169
lasted until 603 when the civil war got resolved
by splitting the Khaganate into two.

00:02:14.169 --> 00:02:17.340
The Western Turkic Khaganate and the Eastern
Turkic Khaganate.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.569
The Eastern Turkic Khaganate was then subdued
by the Tang Dynasty in 630 becoming their

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:23.569
vassals.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:29.310
In the west the Bulgars rebelled against the
Avars in 632 establishing the Old Great Bulgaria.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.340
During that time with the fall of the Eastern
Turkic Khaganate, the Western Turkic Khaganate

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.160
wasn’t fairing any better and in around
the 630s it started to lose control over the

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.329
various nomadic tribes living within its borders,
the most notable of these tribes were the

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.329
Khazars.

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:47.950
The Khazars broke off from the control of
the Western Turkic Khaganate at some point

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:53.079
between 630 and 650 consolidating power south
of the Volga river.

00:02:53.079 --> 00:02:58.010
Once they emerged as a consolidated polity
they started to look outwards trying to conquer

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.819
the Bulgars to the West, the Kangar Union
to the East and also fighting the Arabs to

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:03.819
the south.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:08.510
The Kangar Union was a collection of various
nomadic tribes that, under the leadership

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:13.159
of the Kangars, rebelled against the Western
Turkic Khaganate when it was invaded and subdued

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.980
by the Tang dynasty in 657.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:21.800
In 668 after the death of their Khagan the
Old Great Bulgaria finally succumbed to the

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.409
Khazars with some of the Bulgars migrating
North and Establishing Volga Bulgaria and

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:30.269
some migrating west and establishing the First
Bulgarian Kingdom.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:36.230
In 682 the Gokturks of the Eastern Turkic
Khaganate, who were the vassals of the Tang,

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.579
successfully rebelled against the Chinese
and started to consolidate power in the steppe

00:03:40.579 --> 00:03:41.579
once again.

00:03:41.579 --> 00:03:45.919
In 712 they conquered what remained of the
Western Turkic Khaganate, which was now called

00:03:45.919 --> 00:03:50.799
the Turgesh Khaganate as the Turgesh took
control of the Khaganate away from the Gokturks.

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:55.159
With this conquest of the Turgesh Khaganate
the Gokturks of the Eastern Turkic Khaganate

00:03:55.159 --> 00:03:58.779
formed what we call today the Second Turkic
Khaganate.

00:03:58.779 --> 00:04:03.129
During the formation of the Second Turkic
Khaganate the Gokturks violently subdued a

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:08.040
nomadic tribe called the Uyghurs who subsequently
started to plot against them.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.930
Also around the late 7th century the Umayyad
forces took control of the Amu and Syr darya

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:17.890
rivers away from the Kangar Union and in the
early 8th century the Arabs came into conflict

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.670
with the Tang Empire over the valuable trading
area of Sogdia.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:26.500
This fighting was marked with frequent involvement
of the various local nomadic tribes from the

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.060
Second Turkic Khaganate, most notably the
Turgesh and the Oghuz.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:36.220
In 744 the Uyghurs, now with new allies, led
a rebellion against the Gokturks and overthrew

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.100
them ending the Second Turkic Khaganate.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.380
Subsequently the Uyghurs established a new
nomadic polity known as the Uyghur Khaganate.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.820
As part of consolidating power within this
new Khaganate the Uyghurs attacked one of

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.730
their allies that helped them overthrow the
Gokturks, the Karluks.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:56.470
After this attack the Karluks migrated west
to the land of the Oghuz and the Turgesh who

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.850
they defeated and took control of their land.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:04.590
The Turgesh assimilated into the Karluks while
the defeated Oghuz had no choice but to migrate

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.440
west into the Kangar Union.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:11.670
There the Oghuz allied with the Kimaks, who
were under Kangar control, and overthrew the

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.670
Kangars.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:16.851
The defeated Kangars united with the remaining
tribes still loyal to them and formed a new

00:05:16.851 --> 00:05:18.680
tribe called the Pechenegs.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:23.760
The Pechenegs subsequently migrated westwards
fighting off the Khazars and settling around

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.820
the Ural river.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.830
The victorious Oghuz and Kimaks then divided
the Kangar lands and formed their own polities

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.220
in the area in c. 750.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.290
These polities were called the Kimak Khaganate
and the Oghuz Yabgu State.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:41.420
Oghuz also managed to reconquer some parts
of the Syr Darya river from the Arabs and

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.970
the Uyghurs managed to get hold of some Sogdian
trading cities.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:50.490
This is where I will end the VERY oversimplified
summary of the early medieval Euroasian Steppe.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:56.190
Keep in mind that the sources about this area
and this period are very sparse and, therefore,

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:00.530
the details of these events are very much
still debated today by historians.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.840
Due to that some historians may present slightly
different versions of events that occurred

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.500
in this area during this time, specially when
it comes to territorial control of the various

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:14.280
polities mentioned as that is probably one
of the hardest things to pinpoint.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.960
With that said, now that you’re more confused
than ever about the history of the Euroasian

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.950
steppe, we can delve into the lifestyles of
the people that lived in this land of constant

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.950
flux.

